Troubleshooting
Problem
Fix
PowerShell prompts for Name: when creating users
You ran the New-ADUser commands before defining $password. Run the entire script block at once — the $password line must come first. Copy the full block from Step 4 and run it all together.
Cannot copy and paste into the VM
Open the RDP client on your local machine, click Show Options → Local Resources tab, check Clipboard. Reconnect. Or download the RDP file from the Azure portal and open it with the native Remote Desktop app instead of using the browser.
Promotion fails: DNS conflict
Set the NIC's preferred DNS to 127.0.0.1 before promoting, or use the static IP of the VM
Cannot RDP after domain join
Log in as LAB\Administrator (domain admin) not just Administrator
GPO not applying
Run gpupdate /force on the target machine, then gpresult /r to see applied policies
User cannot log in after creation
Confirm the account is Enabled and ChangePasswordAtLogon is set
AD Users and Computers not showing
Run: dsa.msc from the Run dialog, or run: Add-WindowsFeature RSAT-ADDS




